meta {
  name: Patient Context (/patient)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/patient
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.patientId: isString
}

docs {
  UC-1 (REQUIREMENTS.md), and the tail of the UC-6 drill-down: the launched patient's identity plus
  problem/medication/allergy reachability, the one data call behind the per-patient landing
  confirmation (`PatientEndpoints`, REQUIREMENTS.md's pre-visit-brief entry point). Reads whatever
  PatientSessionContext is already in the session the `sessionCookie` cookie names - either a direct
  single-patient `/launch` -> `/callback`, or Select Patient.bru's drill-down (same cookie, no
  separate login). With no PatientSessionContext, PatientEndpoints.HandleGetPatientAsync returns 401
  before reaching OpenEMR, so these assertions fail closed rather than reporting green with nothing
  behind them.
}
